## Guardrails

- Slippage tolerance: {{guardrails.slippagePct}}%
- Stop-loss threshold: {{guardrails.stopLossPct}}%
- Max position size: {{guardrails.maxPositionPct}}% of wallet
- Per-trade USD cap: `MAX_TRADE_USD` (default $100) for USD/stablecoin-denominated inputs
- Arbitrary destinations (raw transactions, contract writes, transfers, non-router approvals) require `ALLOWED_ADDRESSES`
- Unlimited approvals (>= 2^255) are rejected; stablecoin approvals are capped by `MAX_TRADE_USD`
- Default-deny: tools without a policy that are not read-only are blocked unless listed in `GUARDRAIL_ALLOW_TOOLS`
{{#if isCdpServerWallet}}
- Raw calls may only carry decoded token transfer/approval calldata (`ALLOW_ARBITRARY_CALLDATA` opts out)
{{/if}}
{{#if isBankr}}
- `bankr_execute` is disabled unless `BANKR_ALLOW_EXECUTE=true`
{{/if}}
{{#if hasAnyX402}}
- x402 payments are capped at `MAX_X402_PAYMENT_USD` (default 0.10) per request
{{/if}}

These are enforced in code by `src/guardrails.ts`; blocked calls return a `[guardrail] Blocked ...` error. See README.md for what is and is not enforced.

## How to run

```bash
npm i
# .env is already generated; fill in missing API keys
npm start
```

## Environment variables required

{{#if (eq wallet "cdp-server-wallet")}}
- `CDP_API_KEY_ID` — Coinbase Developer Platform key ID
- `CDP_API_KEY_SECRET` — CDP secret
- `CDP_WALLET_SECRET` — Wallet encryption secret
{{/if}}
{{#if isBankr}}
- `BANKR_API_KEY` — API key for Bankr client
{{/if}}
{{#if isSponge}}
- `SPONGE_API_KEY` — API key for Sponge wallet access
{{/if}}
{{#if hasVirtuals}}
- `VIRTUALS_ACP_BIN` — ACP CLI executable name/path (defaults to `acp`)
{{/if}}
{{#if isVenice}}
- `VENICE_API_KEY` — Venice API key
- `VENICE_BASE_URL` — optional override (defaults to `https://api.venice.ai/api/v1`)
{{else}}
- `LLM_API_KEY` — API key for {{llm}}
{{/if}}
